 "definition": "Printing in which a head of small pins strikes an inked ribbon to form characters and images from patterns of dots.",
 "description": {
  "text": "A computer printing process, also called impact matrix printing, that applies ink using a low-resolution dot matrix. Dot matrix printers are impact printers that print with a fixed number of pins or wires on a moving print head.",
